{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 1, :comments ["<b>And He called.</b> We find an individual covenant on account of two things, and it is possible for a single commandment to be on account of many things, like the commandment of the burnt offering and the sacrifice, for by giving each portion in its time, the portion that has a share in the World to Come escapes. Therefore the meaning of לכפר is to give ransom, and the witness is from the beginning of כי תשא, for which reason it is written פן יפגענו בדבר. Also there are in the burnt offerings secrets for the futures, and from every sacrifice one may contemplate the secret of the generations and the sin offerings and the commandments, to give life to the teachers of Torah. The sense of <b>and He called to Moses</b> is after ולא יכול משה, that the Glory called him from the Tent of Meeting, that he should come there, and there He would speak with him. And the Glory was inside the curtain, and there Moses would enter, for so it is written, and this is the meaning of ותמונת ה׳ יביט. The reason for mentioning the sacrifices before the commandments is that the Shekhinah would return to its place if they do not keep the law of the burnt offering — and so it was — and far be it, far be it to need a burnt offering. And so it is written, אם ארעב לא אומר לך. Only, it has a secret:"], :book :leviticus, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 1, :notes {0 "ויקרא and לא יכול משה refer to Exodus 40:35; ותמונת ה׳ יביט to Numbers 12:8; פן יפגענו בדבר to Exodus 5:3; אם ארעב לא אומר לך to Psalm 50:12. The verse references are implicit in the Hebrew and resolved here."}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:08:25.921075986Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}